	"rows": [
		{
			"id": "e-DUQph2c9GclUDV2",
			"description": "Lascannon",
			"local_notes": "Needs a tripod or vehicle pit mount (ST 14M): an unmounted human cannot brace it, though Astartes ST lets a Space Marine fire it standing (treat as braced at ST 14 rather than mounted, GM's call). The 80 lb is the weapon alone; the tripod (Heavy Weapon Tripod, 20 lb) is extra. Draws from a dedicated power cell (see Lascannon Power Cell); swapping cells takes the 5-turn reload noted in shots.\n\nLore: The definitive Imperial anti-tank weapon: Guard heavy weapons squads, Space Marine Devastators and Predator/Razorback/Land Raider sponsons and turrets all mount it, and Black Library fiction (Gaunt's Ghosts, Horus Heresy novels) consistently has a well-placed lascannon shot cripple or kill a battle tank, and treats it as one of the few man-portable weapons that can bring down a Terminator or walker.\n\nDesign: Damage is the fixed anchor from framework.md: 8dx8(5) burn (\"kills tanks and Terminators\"). Checked against the vehicle AV table with the exact dice distribution: average 224 burn through an armor divisor of 5 gives an effective DR of 20 (AV10) to 70 (AV14). Even the minimum roll (8 dice all at 1, x8 = 64) clears every effective DR on the table except AV14's 70, which it misses only when all eight dice show 1 (1 in 1.7 million), so the lascannon beats AV10 through AV14 (DR 100-350) essentially every time with the anchor's divisor doing almost all the work; against a Terminator (DR 200, effective DR 40) or Astartes power armor (DR 100, effective DR 20) it is a guaranteed penetration (minimum roll 64), matching \"kills tanks and Terminators\" without exception. Acc, range, RoF, shots, Bulk and Rcl are not anchored by framework.md, so they're built from first principles: RoF 1 and Rcl 1 because a beam weapon has no recoil and the capacitor cycle time is the limiting factor; Acc 14 and a long 1500/4500 range because the weapon's entire battlefield role is precision fire on distant armor, which demands better optics than a lasgun (Acc 6); Bulk -8 and ST 14M (sqrt(10x80)=28, mostly carried by the mount) because the weapon and its cooling housing are backpack-sized and unwieldy without a brace. Cost and LC follow \"military-issue heavy weapons\" (LC2) and are priced well above a lasgun to reflect scarcity of the long-barrel focusing crystal.",
