		{
			"id": "eGuN7Vv92kT-L1H3J",
			"description": "Autocannon",
			"local_notes": "Weight includes the tripod mount; a Heavy Weapons Squad crews it as gunner plus loader. The Predator battle tank's turret gun is the same weapon on a stabilised vehicle mount.\n\nLore: The autocannon is the Guard heavy weapons squad's and the Predator tank's main anti-light-vehicle gun throughout the fiction: reliably described tearing through Ork trukks, light xenos raiders and Sentinel-class walkers, denting Rhinos and Chimeras, and bouncing or only chipping a Leman Russ or Land Raider's frontal glacis.\n\nDesign: Not covered by a framework anchor, so it's built as a solid-projectile \"stub\" weapon per the TL table (autogun/stubber bracket, scaled to artillery-grade tolerances) rather than borrowed from any GURPS catalogue cannon: a single heavy AP penetrator per round gives pi++ (full wound multiplier, no follow-up), with a moderate armor divisor (3) for the hardened long-rod core. Checked with the exact dice distribution (6dx3(3) pi++, avg 63) against the vehicle AV table: it penetrates AV10 (DR 100, eff. DR 33) 99% of the time and AV11 (DR 150, eff. DR 50, a Rhino's front/sides) 85% of the time - reliably beats both, as required; against AV12 (DR 200, eff. DR 66, a Chimera's front) that drops to 36% - sometimes beats it, matching \"dents a Rhino, sometimes cracks a Chimera\"; and against AV13 (DR 275, eff. DR 91) it falls to 1% and AV14 (DR 350, eff. DR 116) to effectively 0% - it does not beat a Leman Russ or Land Raider's armour, matching every source that has autocannon fire shrug off a main battle tank's frontal plate. Handling: RoF 5 - a real chain-driven or revolver-cannon autoloader cycles noticeably faster than a bolter's semi/burst RoF 3, but this project keeps it well under the true chain-gun rate of the Assault Cannon (RoF 20) and the rapid-emitter Multi-laser (RoF 9), so the autocannon reads as a burst-fire cannon rather than a spray-weapon, matching its lore role of putting a few large, accurate rounds into a specific target rather than hosing an area. ST 14M (mounted) and Bulk -8 are unchanged.",
