		{
			"id": "el-umskU03aBp8pY3",
			"description": "Assault Cannon",
			"local_notes": "Arm- or hip-socket mounted on Terminator armour, or carried and fired one-handed by an Astartes on a stabilising harness; ST 15 assumes Astartes-grade strength rather than a tripod.\n\nLore: Terminators, Dreadnoughts and vehicle sponsons (Predators, Land Raiders) use the multi-barrelled assault cannon (the Chaos Soulreaper cannon is the same design) as a close-to-mid-range storm of solid shot for shredding infantry, light vehicles and swarms; it is fired solid rounds rather than bolts, which is why it sits outside the bolt-weapon family, and fiction almost always pairs it with a melee specialist (power fist, thunder hammer) on the same Terminator rather than relying on it against tanks.\n\nDesign: No framework anchor, so it's built parallel to the heavy bolter anchor ((8d+2)x2(2) pi++, follow-up 2d+2 cr ex) rather than copied from it: the assault cannon fires solid rotary-autocannon-style rounds with no explosive follow-up and a lower pi+ wound multiplier (dense solid shot, not a mass-reactive bolt), so it drops the follow-up term and scales the base damage down (5d instead of 8d+2) in exchange for a much higher RoF (20 vs. the heavy bolter's 8; framework.md puts assault cannons at 15-20+), matching its fluff role as a horde-clearing hail of fire rather than a hard-hitting single line of shots. Checked with the exact dice distribution (5dx2(2) pi+, avg 35) against the vehicle AV table: even at RoF 20, no single round reliably clears AV10's effective DR 50 (only 1.6% per shot), so it cannot reliably beat any vehicle on the table - consistent with Astartes fiction, where the assault cannon is a horde/infantry weapon and its wielder relies on a paired melee weapon (power fist, thunder hammer) or a squadmate's lascannon/missile launcher against real armour. LC1 follows the framework's Astartes-gear bracket (alongside bolters and plasma) rather than the Guard's LC2 heavy-weapon bracket.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
			"tech_level": "10",
			"legality_class": "1",
			"base_value": "20000",
			"base_weight": "55 lb",
