		{
			"id": "epJ5arNy0SkduUU6Y",
			"description": "Mortar",
			"local_notes": "Baseplate, bipod and tube break down for a three-man crew to carry; minimum range about 20 yd (the bomb's arming distance, not a targeting limit). Uses the indirect-fire rules under Artillery, not a direct line of sight.\n\nLore: The mortar is the Guard's simplest and most ubiquitous indirect-fire support weapon, issued down to platoon level in Guard fiction for exactly the reason real-world mortars are: cheap, rugged, easy to manufacture on almost any forge world, and effective against dug-in infantry and soft targets beyond line of sight.\n\nDesign: No framework anchor, so it's placed at the bottom of the TL table deliberately - mortar tube technology is older and simpler than lasguns, stubbers or rockets, which is exactly why every regiment from a hive world to a feral-world levy can field one. Damage is built the same way as the missile launcher's frag warhead (B414 fragmentation, \"big frag grenade\" scaling) with the fragmentation doubled again over a hand grenade's 6d (12d cut, against the missile's 9d), since a mortar bomb is not weight-constrained by a rocket motor and can devote more of its mass to filler and casing, giving 6dx2 cr ex [12d cut]. Basic Set Artillery specialties have no Mortar entry, so it uses Artillery (Cannon). It carries no armor divisor and is not intended to be checked against the vehicle AV table at all - its role in the fiction is area denial and infantry suppression, not armour-killing, so unlike the autocannon, krak missile or lascannon above it has no reliably/ sometimes/cannot-beat line against AV10-14.",
