		{
			"id": "e66mz9NuSKqA5DBHf",
			"description": "Battle Cannon",
			"local_notes": "Vehicle mount only (the Leman Russ turret). One shell at a time from a loader's hands: 6 seconds to reload alone, half that with the loader at work. A direct hit does full damage and bursts; everyone nearby takes the blast (B414) and the fragments (B414).\n\nLore: The Leman Russ's main gun, a heavy smooth-bore cannon firing high-explosive shells: in the wargame a Strength 8, AP3 large blast that flattens infantry, kills Space Marines outright and punches through the side and rear armour of most tanks but bounces off a Leman Russ's own front.\n\nDesign: 6dx10 cr ex (avg 210): enough to kill a Marine through power armour (DR 100) on a direct hit, to go through AV10 (DR 125) almost always and AV11 (DR 185) about 70% of the time, AV12 (250) about one hit in seven, and never AV13 (340) or AV14 (440), close to the wargame's Strength 8 against those values. The [6d] fragments are the Basic Set's ratio for a shell this size (B414). Acc 6 and 1500/6000 for a stabilised tank sight on a long gun; Rcl 3 for the recoil of a single heavy round on a 63-tonne hull.",
